  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adaptations to JR</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adaptations to JR</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACC-I2 - Number of adaptations in the design and/or implementation of the JR, as a result of the input from beneficiaries.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Possible in case of change in context or based on community preference</narrative>
    </description>
    <reference code="ACC-I2" indicator-uri="https://www.zoa-international.com" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-06"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project was originally planned to provide vouchers of 204 USD, 143 USD from the ACM project and 61 from other projects/donors. However, upon knowing this the targeted beneficiaries suggested that the funds that come in from other projects should not be given to them but rather to other people in need. Their suggestion was honored by SOS Sahel team, after discussions with ZOA, vouchers with a value of 143 USD were distributed and was able to use the funds from the other project to support additional 200 HHs instead of giving the top-up amount of 61 USD as originally planned to meet 100% of the food basket amount.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Availability of, access to and consumption of food</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Availability of, access to and consumption of food</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">FSC-I2 - Number of people enabled to meet their basic food needs</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3240 vulnerable beneficiaries (540 HH) will receive 3 packages of food consisting of oil, milk, meat, sugar, tomatoes, okra and lentils</narrative>
    </description>
    <reference code="FSC-I2" indicator-uri="https://www.zoa-international.com" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-06"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3240"></target>
     <actual value="3508">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3508 vulnerable beneficiaries  (540HH) received food vouchers to cover food needs for 3 month In North and South Darfur.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
